+class GridPatchDataset(IterableDataset):
+    """
+    Yields patches from images read from an image dataset. The patches are chosen in a contiguous grid sampling scheme.
+
+    Patch geometry is provided by a patch generator (``patch_iter``, e.g. :py:class:`PatchIter`), which takes one
+    image item and yields ``(patch, coordinates)`` tuples. Each patch can then be transformed individually by
+    `transform`. With ``with_coordinates=True`` (the default) each element is a ``(patch, coordinates)`` pair, where
+    ``coordinates`` is an integer array of shape ``(ndim, 2)`` holding the start and stop of each dimension of the
+    patch in the original image, including the channel dimension (first row ``[0, C]``).
+
+    Example:
+
